# 0014. RFID through the lid: module flipped, ≤ 1 cm to the card

Date: 2026-11-06
Status: Accepted

## Context
The card is read through the top of the enclosure. RC522 range with an
ISO card is typically 3–5 cm in free air; metal near the antenna (speaker
magnet, LED strip copper, screws) detunes it and can halve that.

## Decision
- RC522 module mounted **component side down**: header pins point into the
  box, the card reads through the bare back of the PCB (+1.6 mm).
- Lid thickness + air gap to the PCB **≤ 10 mm**.
- **No metal over the antenna footprint**; LED strip around the card area
  with ≥ 10 mm clearance from the coil edge; speaker as far from the
  antenna as the layout allows.
- Range not measured with spacers; verified once with a 1 cm paper stack
  (center and corner) before the lid is printed.

## Consequences
- Lid and module mount are designed together; the module needs a flat seat
  directly under the card area.
- If the final build reads unreliably, the first suspect is metal near the
  coil, not the lid thickness.